        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Just want to clarify: I use global sessions that live in synced folder and local sessions in git repos. Thus, I can share both global and local sessions. The only problem is absolute paths in session files, which can be patched to relative after the session file is written.\r\nWhat do you think about this scheme? Any pitfalls?\r\nIs there any vim event that I can hook to before you provide the post-write function? \r\n",
            "created_at": "2022-04-29T14:34:17Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/67#issuecomment-1113396724",
            "id": 1113396724,
